#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/hu.rc -- Hungarian, the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "hu"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block, in the order of en.rc; app.rc includes this file. The rules every table obeys stand in
// l10n/RULES.md; where each string is seen and how much room it has is res/lang/context.tsv;
// tests/l10n.rs holds this file to en.rc.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.
//
// Hungarian: o and u with a double acute (U+0151, U+0171), never the circumflex or tilde forms;
// quotes are „…” and the dash is the en dash, as in Windows; the user is addressed formally
// (Kattintson, Nyomja meg). After {0} the support word with "a(z)" stands before it, so that no
// case suffix is ever put on a substituted value (RULES 17).

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Hungarian — `[general] language = "hu"`. LANG_HUNGARIAN 0x0E.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
